hypothesis: The one lever we have never combined with distillation is EPOCH COUNT
  on top of his cited batch size. v022/v023 ran 3 epochs; his notes say 5. Everything
  else is v023, which is our best entry (0.6568 public) and which the public board
  showed is TIED with the 42%-larger v022, so student size is settled and is not where
  the remaining 0.0109 to 0.6677 lives. This tests whether training LONGER on the
  same teacher closes any of it, at a cost of ~2.5 h rather than the ~8 h it would
  have taken before the batch-64 speedup.
